Explanation of statistical indicators 

Goods - any movable property, including currency and currency values, electric, 
thermal and other types of energy, vehicles (with the exception of vehicles used to 
transport passengers and goods, including containers and other transport equipment), 
intellectual property; 
Export of goods - the export of goods from the customs territory of the Republic of 
Uzbekistan without an obligation to re-import them, unless otherwise provided by law; 
Re-export - a customs regime in which foreign goods are exported from the c ustoms 
territory; 
Import of goods - the import of goods into the customs territory of the Republic of 
Uzbekistan without an obligation to re-export them; 
Re-import - a regime in which goods of the Republic of Uzbekistan imported from 
the customs territory in the export regime are imported back within the time limits 
established by the Customs Code of the Republic of Uzbekistan (within ten years from the 
date of export); 
Foreign trade turnover - the sum of the values of export and import of a country for 
a certain period; 
Country of origin of goods  - the country in which the goods were completely 
produced or subjected to sufficient processing (criteria for sufficient processing of goods 
are determined in accordance with Article 26 of the Law of the Republic  of Uzbekistan 
“On Customs Tariff”); 
Country of destination of goods  - a country known at the time of shipment as the 
final country of destination of goods; 
Statistical value of goods  - the sum of the value of goods under a contract reduced 
to a single basis, regardless of the currency of the contract; 
CIF (cost, insurance, freight) - a condition for the sale of goods, according to which 
the price of the goods includes its cost and the costs of insurance and transportation of 
goods to the port of the importing country; 
CIP (freight / transportation and insurance)  - a condition for th e sale of goods, 
according to which the price of the goods includes its cost, insurance and transportation 
costs to the destination on the border of the importing country;
